WHAT: Replaces SolEncoder cursor-based encoding with direct mem::alloc +
encode_to_ptr for event data encoding in the HIR lowering.

WHY: Event emission was going through the full SolEncoder abstraction
(alloc cursor, advance cursor, write words), which generates multiple
obj.alloc + obj.store operations. Direct encoding skips the cursor overhead.

GAS IMPACT: -957 gas total.
  amm/swapAForB: -408
  amm/addLiquidity: -312
  erc20/transfer: -58
  erc20/approve: -38
  governance: -9 to -26
  amm/getK: -11

TEAM NOTES: This is a Fe lowering change (hir/src/core/lower/event.rs), not
a std library change. It optimizes event emission at the compiler level by
generating more efficient IR directly. AMM benefits most because swap/addLiq
emit events with multiple parameters. Contracts without events see no change.
